# Environment
#
# `.env` matches that name and nothing else — not `.env.bak`, not
# `.env.bak.20260728_030003`. A hand-made backup beside it was therefore an
# untracked, *unignored* copy of every production secret sitting in a checkout
# of a public repository (#27). The glob below is deliberately wide: anything
# whose name starts with `.env` is assumed to hold what `.env` holds.
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.env.bak

# Any *other* file whose name ends in `.env`, for the same reason one directory
# down: `backup.env` holds the object-store credentials and the restic password
# (#4), it lives in /opt/kolonie because that is where the systemd unit reads it
# from, and /opt/kolonie is a checkout of this public repository. None of the
# patterns above match it — `.env.*` matches names that *start* with `.env`.
#
# `.env.example` is unaffected: it does not end in `.env`.
*.env

# Traefik
traefik/acme.json
traefik/acme-staging.json

# htpasswd lines for the basicAuth middlewares in traefik/dynamic/routes.yml,
# mounted into the Traefik container as /secrets (#30). Traefik cannot read an
# environment variable from a dynamic config file, so a password hash has to
# arrive as a file — and this is a checkout of a public repository.
secrets/

# Docker
docker-compose.override.yml

# Written on the deploy host by scripts/deploy.sh, never committed.
#
# `docker-compose.last.yml` is the one that matters: `docker compose config`
# interpolates, so before #27 it rendered JWT_SECRET, POSTGRES_PASSWORD,
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, HCAPTCHA_SECRET and GITHUB_VERIFIER_TOKEN in cleartext
# into the checkout on every deploy. It is written with --no-interpolate now, so
# this is defence in depth rather than the fix — but the fix and the ignore both
# belong here, because the next person to add a snapshot will reach for `config`
# without the flag.
docker-compose.last.yml
backups/
state/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs
*.log
logs/
